-The kubepods parent cgroup slice on node {{ $labels.instance }} (the node label is 'instance' on node-exporter series) has recorded own-limit OOM kill(s) in the last 1h. memory.events.local counts ONLY kills caused by the PARENT slice breaching its own ceiling — a container breaching its OWN limit lands in the hierarchical counter instead and is covered by ContainerOOMKilled — so the victim here was WITHIN its limit and was killed anyway: the pod limits on this node now sum past the kubepods slice ceiling. A memory-limit raise has overshot. The correct response is to REVERT that raise, NOT to raise anything further (raising again enlarges the overshoot). This is a rolling 1h window, so the revert silences it once the kills stop — no node reboot needed. Read the raw cumulative counter with: talosctl -e <node-ip> -n <node-ip> read /sys/fs/cgroup/kubepods/memory.events.local
