index f84bdbee0c833f905489475da8ef57c83241c7bd..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
--- a/infrastructure/alerts/pages/macbook-inference-probe-stale.alert.description.txt
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1 +0,0 @@
-macbook_inference_pool_serving has had no fresh series for 30m while the workstation (the probe host) is up, so the pool-unreachable alert is blind (the #15577 self-checking guard). What wrote that metric was `ops inference pool-probe`, run by macbook-inference-probe.timer. That command went with the ops CLI and akasha carries no replacement — `pool-probe` is in no command, no unit and no file in the tree — so nothing has written the metric since. This therefore fires on an absence that will not fill until the probe is built again, which is a decision rather than a repair. Check: systemctl --user status macbook-inference-probe.timer on the workstation, to see whether the timer is still firing at nothing.
